# Grammar for the sofiia-grounded-json-v0.2 contract, where the answer is a
# list of claims and each claim names the segments that support it.
#
# v0.2 of this grammar holds the flat shape - one answer string and one list
# of citations beside it - and that is still what config/model_*.json and the
# runtime on main expect. This file exists beside it, not over it, so the
# branch moving to per-claim citations has a grammar to move to and nothing
# on main changes underneath it.
#
# Every rule must sit on ONE line. llama.cpp's GBNF parser ends a rule at the
# newline, so a rule body wrapped across lines is a parse error - which reads
# only as "failed to parse grammar" and took a bisect to find.
#
# Key order is fixed and matches the schema's required order: answer, quotes,
# abstain. It costs the model nothing and removes permutations a small model
# spends tokens getting wrong. One to three claims, matching minItems and
# maxItems. Each claim's text is bounded at about 600 characters: three of
# them at that length is already past the 120-word answer limit, so the bound
# stops a runaway without shaping ordinary prose.
#
# The grammar guarantees shape, never truth. Whether a citation names a real
# segment and whether a quote appears in its source is the verifier's job, and
# stays the verifier's job.

root ::= "{" ws "\"answer\":" ws claims "," ws "\"quotes\":" ws quotes "," ws "\"abstain\":" ws boolean "}" ws
claims ::= "[" ws claim ("," ws claim){0,2} "]" ws
claim ::= "{" ws "\"text\":" ws claimstring "," ws "\"citations\":" ws idarray "}" ws
idarray ::= "[" ws ( string ("," ws string)* )? "]" ws
quotes ::= "[" ws ( qitem ("," ws qitem)* )? "]" ws
qitem ::= "{" ws "\"segment_id\":" ws string "," ws "\"text\":" ws string "}" ws
boolean ::= ("true" | "false") ws
string ::= "\"" ( [^"\\\x7F\x00-\x1F] | "\\" (["\\bfnrt] | "u" [0-9a-fA-F]{4}) )* "\"" ws
claimstring ::= "\"" ( [^"\\\x7F\x00-\x1F] | "\\" (["\\bfnrt] | "u" [0-9a-fA-F]{4}) ){1,600} "\"" ws
ws ::= | " " | "\n" [ \t]{0,20}
